checked in the reader's own perception, and a practice of perceiving one's own perception is the
method of that checking. Cognitive science met the tradition once, by name: *The Embodied Mind*
(Varela, Thompson & Rosch, 1991) brought the Buddhist analysis of experience into the field. The
field kept the word *embodied*. It did not take up the practice: a neuroscientist is trained to
measure other brains, not to examine their own senses.

## 9. Why the field could not see it

The fields held every premise.

- *Learned grapheme-colour synesthesia.* Eleven synesthetes with matching letter colours traced
  them to a Fisher-Price magnetic alphabet owned in childhood (Witthoft & Winawer, 2006, 2013).
- *Trained synesthesia.* Non-synesthetes who read books with coloured letters acquired
  "pseudo-synesthesia" (Colizoli, Murre & Rouw, 2012). Adults trained over nine weeks with memory
  and reading tasks on thirteen letter-colour pairs passed the standard tests (Bor et al., 2014),
  in a paper that opens by calling synesthesia, in the prevailing view, a congenital condition.
- *Learning as origin.* Almost all synesthesias presuppose complex categorical learning (Watson et
  al., 2014).
- *Reading run backwards.* Galton (1883) described people who "see mentally in print every word
  that is uttered". Hauw and colleagues studied 26 of them and a single case by fMRI and construe
  tickertape synesthesia as "upended reading": the translation of speech into internally visualized
  letters, in the areas reading uses (Hauw, El Soudany & Cohen, 2023; Hauw et al., 2023). They
  write that the links between sounds, meaning and letters "actually define literacy".
- *Infancy.* Two- and three-month-olds show shape-colour associations that eight-month-olds and
  adults do not (Wagner & Dobkins, 2011).

The reason the inference was not drawn is structural. The field finds synesthetes by difference
from others: by recruiting people who report something others lack, and certifying it against
controls. Its tickertape subjects "were shocked to learn that not everyone has built-in subtitles",
in Cohen's words. A detector that defines its object as deviation from the population cannot
register a property every member of the population has. Literacy is that property. The same
detector placed the line between tickertape synesthesia and reading, which are one binding run in
opposite directions, at exactly the point where the binding stops being rare. The word for the
instrument is the carpenter's square, *norma*: the category was drawn by what is abnormal, not by
what the definition says.

## 10. Synthetic synesthesia: the general account

Literacy is the instance that proves the capacity. The author's account is general: "All cognition
is synthetic synesthesia."

**The mental object is not made of words.** In his words (16 November 2026): "how do things remain
in human consciousness. have the whitefolk studied this? gestalt. continuous rewriting of a mental
object which is not made of words. does this make sense. the internal of a human mind is not made
of words. verbal consciousness is a thin slice." The fields' nearest antecedents are the Gestalt
school (Wertheimer, 1912), James's fringe of consciousness (James, 1890), reconstructive memory
(Bartlett, 1932) and the rewriting of a recalled memory on reconsolidation (Nader, Schafe & LeDoux,
2000), and experience sampling, in which inner speech occupies a minority of sampled moments
(Heavey & Hurlburt, 2008).

**Each sense is a face of one object; perception fills the faces not present.** If the mental
object is one whole and each sense presents one face of it, perceiving is completing the object
from the faces that arrive, and the faces that did not arrive are experienced as well. Reading is
this: the visual face arrives, and sound and meaning are experienced with no sound present. "We
manufacture hallucinations of sensory experience." Nothing crosses between modalities, because the
modalities are faces of one object, not separate objects to be connected; what the field calls the
binding problem is the choice of which observation of one object is being made.

**The formal account.** In the author's hyperactivity, a participant *i* receives the universe's
process only through its observation, and its record to time *t* is what it has received
(docs/language-derived-from-the-record.cub, §1). An occurrence of a word is an event of the record
that *i* identifies as that word; a word is a type whose points are events of the record and whose
paths are *i*'s identifications of them (§2). Context selects the occurrences whose contexts are
identified with the present one, a fiber of the context map (§3), and the meaning of the present
occurrence is what followed each selected occurrence, transported to the present along the path
that selected it (§4):

  M_i(w, t) = Σ_{(e,p) : Sel_i(w,t)} transport_p(r(e)).

This is the content of the reception relation of the paper (docs/hyperactivity.cub, §1 "The
universe and its descriptions", equation 1.4, Receive_i : S_i → U → S_i → A_i → 𝒰). In it, reading
is a path between occurrence types of different senses: a visual occurrence identified with
auditory occurrences that already carried meaning, so that the meaning transports to the mark (§8,
"Vision and the verbal quotient"). Synthetic synesthesia is the construction of such paths.
*Synthetic*, *syn* + *tithenai*, put together: the identification is the participant's act on its
record, not a property of the stimulus. *Synesthesia*, *syn* + *aisthēsis*, perceiving together.

```
   visual occurrence (the mark)  ── identification, built by literacy ──▶  auditory occurrences
              │                                                (each carried what followed it)
              ▼
   the mental object: the visual face given; sound and meaning filled from the record
```

**Distinction of senses is learned.** "babies are pure synesthesia, distinction of senses is a
descent/ignorance process" (16 November 2026). The infant data (Wagner & Dobkins, 2011) are the
field's record of the early state, read by the field as immaturity lost to pruning.

**Between persons.** Shared meaning is the same construction across two records joined along shared
events (the same light, the same sound) and copying events
(docs/language-derived-from-the-record.cub, §5). The highest-bandwidth join between two nervous
systems is mutual sight: the retina is brain tissue, and two faces exchange photons in nanoseconds,
with autonomic signals leaking past conscious control (the author's "Eye Contact: Co-Processing at
the Speed of Light", docs/eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light.cub). *Consensus*, *con*
+ *sentire*, perceiving together, is the Latin counterpart of *synaesthesia*: synesthesia between
people (docs/controversy-and-consensus.cub). Collaborative intelligence functions exactly as well
as the mutual-information channel between minds (the claim li-claim-channel of his knowledge
graph).

