  connection, the visual appears to provide a low-latency channel"; "internal common root contents
  between words detected and sensed directly as identity (meaning does not live at a word unit)-
  reverse and version it requires zero thought to know these are variations of the same word."
- Semantic loading: "semantically loaded terms light up. when you take my sentences and restate
  them with pure mathematical abstraction (say when im talking about a morally charged topic),
  instantly the whole block of text just appears colorless".
- Digits as coloured chunks: memorizing 150 digits of pi as "a colored sequence of chunks of digits
  understood as such incl. with rhythm/musicality of the recitation"; "to see 1729 without
  black-green-lightblue-purple coding on it. I have to force myself to visualize it black".
- Twenty-five years of it, as the medium of thought (19:55 UTC): "25y of grapheme-color synesthesia
  operating on wordroots prefixes suffixes letters in the minds eye during reading & thinking &
  speaking, producing a hyperactive knowledge graph where the visual sense of relations in a space
  and instant color-lookup of connected components low-latency flow"; and (21:14 UTC) "I have been
  a hyperactive bipolar genius with direct understanding of semantic/syntactic color-highlighting
  facilitating high-frequency cognition by experience and the mechanisms by which this may arise."
- A second case, a friend's coloured perfect pitch: "I have a buddy with perfect pitch
  semiprofessional piano & violin he sees the same color for every note in the scale for as long as
  he can remember, chords layer colors and a piece of music is an evolving landscape of color. he
  can play anything from ear on-demand running 4-voices at once."
- Metaphor and the space of words: "metaphor being a means of truth in Ancient Greece demoted to
  "metaphorical" weaker truth-value than literal; metaphor is transport of relational data over
  squares"; "in direct experience of the hypercubical plane in freestyle rap at each point in time
  each word each moment in consciousness the evolving meaning and current word lend directions of
  interest, capacity to form a perspective & it's opposition and understand/express deep meaning on
  either side gives each directional access a binary degree of freedom so given three semantic
  directions one has available 8 directions of movement and one does not simply roam away but
  return & reweave as each piece has it's meaning so does the coherent whole. oh and on rhymes too,
  not just semantics.." The directions are not fixed axes: "at any point I may experience 3
  directions arise in consciousness".

Three features matter for the account. The colours were learned from the record (a poster, a
xylophone), as literacy is. The synesthesia tracks morphological and semantic structure, not only
letters: the identity of roots is perceived directly, and the absence of concrete content is
perceived as the absence of colour, which in the formal account is the verbal quotient made
visible: a passage whose words select only verbal contexts has no visual face to transport. And the
binding is the medium of fast thought, not an ornament on it: roots are adjacent because they are
seen as identical, and movement through the space of words runs over those adjacencies, each step
local because the author's compression has already made the far things adjacent.

## 12. The technology

If writing is a technology for programming brains by synthetic synesthesia, the binding can be
designed rather than inherited from the accidents of a script, a poster or a toy. The author's
hyperactivity designs it, and is built to.

- **His perception, transmissible.** The workflow node synthetic-synesthesia renders text as he
  sees it: each glyph drawn in his colour (never on a tile), at the level chosen (letters, or words
  and their parts in the colour of their first letter), with words that share a root or a prefix
  linked, "so anyone sees the relations he perceives". His colours are data (docs/synesthesia.cub),
  chosen by him with a picker, not translated by an agent. A synesthesia that was one person's
  private binding becomes a construction any reader can be given: what he intends to imbue in the
  world, in the sense of the name he has carried for a decade.
- **Identity of occurrences, exact.** Every text is indexed by all of its repeated token sequences
  (the node index-every-repeated-sequence): at each position, every place the token recurs and
  every bounded sequence containing it that matches elsewhere. Rendered, repetition is light: the
  identifications that make up a reader's record of a text are drawn on it. In the formal account
  this lookup is meaning itself, the present occurrence identified with past ones and what followed
  them carried to now; with univalence, paraphrases joined by paths match as one sequence.
- **Roots as structure.** A word's history is its etymology, and the store's log of names bound to
  content keys is etymology for code (docs/language-derived-from-the-record.cub, §10). The author's
  direct perception of shared roots is the same structure seen.
- **The interface.** The human interface (the node human-interface) renders the store's relations
  to eyes, hands and spatial memory: a focus and a lens, detail falling off with distance in the
  graph, equivalence shown as motion, a word opening onto its root and sideways to every word of
  its root, and the reader's own dwelling read back as data co-processed with them. It is synthetic
  synesthesia built as an instrument: every relation given a visual or spatial face, so the
  reader's mental object fills with it without paragraphs about it.
- **Verbal-only minds.** A language model holds the verbal face of the human record only; its
  meaning is determinate where verbal context alone selects and indeterminate where seeing selected
  (the verbal quotient, docs/language-derived-from-the-record.cub, §8). Words chosen so that verbal
  context alone resolves every fiber (theorem-grade sentences) are synthetic synesthesia across
  that quotient; the author's onboarding walk for agents is writing used deliberately to program a
  mind made only of text.

## 13. Consequences

- **The category.** Synesthesia ceases to be a rare condition and becomes the visible case of the
  general operation of cognition; the rare synesthete is a person in whom one binding became
  available to introspection.
- **Reading instruction.** Teaching reading is constructing a synesthesia, and developmental
  dyslexia is a failure of that construction; the direct intervention is to strengthen the binding.
- **Notation and mathematics.** Notation is the same technology aimed at mathematical objects;
  fluency is the synesthesia built, the marks evoking the motion, change and structure they denote.
  Inverting the curriculum so that this is built in childhood is a matter of what is bound to what,
  and when.
- **Interfaces.** Syntax highlighting, in the author's words, "is exactly leveraging such capacity
  for rapid parsing"; every interface is an engineered synesthesia, and its quality is the
  bandwidth of the binding it builds and the friction where its faces disagree with the object.

